{
  "info": {
    "name": "FixNow Provider Runtime",
    "description": "End-to-end Provider Core Loop (Sprint 5.7).\n\nDrives the full multi-actor narrative:\n  1. Auth — login each of seeker / provider / admin (mobile mode, bearer tokens captured in env vars)\n  2. Admin Provider Approval — approve the provider profile so it can bid\n  3. Seeker Request Creation — the seeker creates a service request\n  4. Provider Available Requests — the provider sees the request in the feed\n  5. Provider Bids — the provider submits a bid\n  6. Seeker Accept Bid — the seeker accepts, which spawns a booking\n  7. Provider Bookings — provider starts and completes the booking\n  8. Notifications — seeker has new notifications, provider can mark-read\n  9. Chat — round-trip: provider opens conversation, sends message, reads back\n  10. Earnings — wallet aggregates reflect the completed booking\n  11. Negative Security — cross-role 403, missing-token 401\n\nBefore running:\n  - Boot the API at http://localhost:4000 (pnpm --filter api dev) with Mailpit running for OTP delivery.\n  - Pre-seed three accounts: seeker, provider (upgraded), admin. The seeded admin user is a project pre-requisite — see docs/testing/provider-runtime-loop.md for the one-time bootstrap recipe.\n  - Copy postman/local.postman_environment.example.json → postman/local.postman_environment.json and fill in the email/password fields for all three accounts.\n  - Run the Auth folder once at the start of every Newman session — it captures seekerToken / providerToken / adminToken into the environment.\n\nEvery response runs the collection-level guard that rejects Prisma / SQL / secret strings.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "fixnow-provider-runtime"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "apiUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000" },
    { "key": "apiVersion", "value": "v1" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const text = pm.response.text();",
          "pm.test('no Prisma/SQL/secret leak', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.match(/PrismaClient|column .* does not exist|SELECT |INSERT |UPDATE /i);",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('passwordHash');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('refreshToken');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('JWT_SECRET');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('DATABASE_URL');",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — Auth",
      "description": "Login each of the three roles in mobile mode. The accessToken from each response is captured into seekerToken / providerToken / adminToken so every later folder can authenticate via {{providerToken}} / {{seekerToken}} / {{adminToken}}.\n\nFor brevity these are direct logins assuming the accounts are already verified. The OTP step is skipped only when AUTH_REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=false in the dev .env (typical local default). If your dev env requires OTP, add a verify-otp request under each login per the auth controller comments.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/auth/login (seeker)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{customerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{customerPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "// Two paths depending on AUTH_REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION:",
                  "//   • dev (false): server returns the auth tokens directly",
                  "//   • prod (true): server returns an OTP challenge — the operator must verify out-of-band",
                  "if (body.tokens && body.tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('seekerToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.test('captured seekerToken', () => pm.expect(body.tokens.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else if (body.otpRequired) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('seekerOtpChallengeId', body.challengeId);",
                  "  pm.test('OTP challenge captured', () => pm.expect(body.challengeId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test.fail('login response carried neither tokens nor OTP challenge');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/auth/login (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{providerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{providerPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.tokens && body.tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('providerToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.test('captured providerToken', () => pm.expect(body.tokens.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else if (body.otpRequired) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('providerOtpChallengeId', body.challengeId);",
                  "  pm.test('OTP challenge captured', () => pm.expect(body.challengeId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test.fail('login response carried neither tokens nor OTP challenge');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/auth/login (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.tokens && body.tokens.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('adminToken', body.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.test('captured adminToken', () => pm.expect(body.tokens.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else if (body.otpRequired) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('adminOtpChallengeId', body.challengeId);",
                  "  pm.test('OTP challenge captured', () => pm.expect(body.challengeId).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test.fail('login response carried neither tokens nor OTP challenge');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/auth/me (seeker)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{seekerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/auth/me"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const me = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('me.id present', () => pm.expect(me.id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('seekerUserId', me.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/me/provider/profile (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/provider/profile"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('profile.id present', () => pm.expect(body.profile.id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('providerProfileId', body.profile.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — Admin Provider Approval",
      "description": "Admin approves the provider profile so it can bid (ProviderActiveGuard requires status=ACTIVE). Idempotent — re-runs that hit an already-ACTIVE profile accept 409 as success.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/admin/providers (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/providers"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array exists', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/admin/providers/:id/approve (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{adminToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/admin/providers/{{providerProfileId}}/approve",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"note\": \"runtime approval\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Idempotent — first run flips DRAFT/PENDING → ACTIVE; re-runs hit",
                  "// 409 because the profile is already ACTIVE. Both are acceptable.",
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 409', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect([200, 201, 204, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 — Seeker Request Creation",
      "description": "The seeker creates a service request. Captures the requestId for the bidding step.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/services (resolve a category id)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/services"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty);",
                  "const cat = body.items.find(c => c.slug === 'plumbing') || body.items[0];",
                  "pm.environment.set('categoryId', cat.id);",
                  "pm.environment.set('categorySlug', cat.slug);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/me/requests (seeker)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{seekerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/requests",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"categoryId\": \"{{categoryId}}\",\n  \"description\": \"runtime test — please ignore\",\n  \"scheduleType\": \"ASAP\",\n  \"manualAddress\": {\n    \"label\": \"Runtime test address\",\n    \"line1\": \"1 Runtime Way\",\n    \"city\": \"Riyadh\",\n    \"country\": \"SA\",\n    \"lat\": 24.7136,\n    \"lng\": 46.6753\n  }\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 201', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const req = body.request || body;",
                  "pm.test('request.id present', () => pm.expect(req.id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('requestId', req.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 — Provider Available Requests",
      "description": "The provider should see the seeker's request in the available-requests feed (ProviderActiveGuard already passed in folder 02).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/provider/available-requests (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/available-requests"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "// Don't fail if the seeker request isn't on page 1 (other test data may exist).",
                  "// The bid step below tolerates that — it submits against {{requestId}} directly."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "05 — Provider Bids",
      "description": "The provider submits a bid against the seeker's request. Captures the bidId for the accept step.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/me/provider/bids (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/provider/bids",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"{{requestId}}\",\n  \"priceQuote\": { \"amount\": 4500, \"currency\": \"USD\", \"pricingType\": \"FIXED\" },\n  \"note\": \"runtime bid\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 201', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const bid = body.bid || body;",
                  "pm.test('bid.id present', () => pm.expect(bid.id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('bidId', bid.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "06 — Seeker Accept Bid",
      "description": "The seeker accepts the provider's bid. The acceptance is what creates the booking; the next folder reads it back via the provider list.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/me/requests/:rid/bids/:bid/accept (seeker)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{seekerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/requests/{{requestId}}/bids/{{bidId}}/accept"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 201', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "07 — Provider Bookings",
      "description": "The provider lists bookings (the accepted bid creates one), then drives it through start → complete.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/me/provider/bookings (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/provider/bookings"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "const target = (body.items || []).find(b => b.bidId === pm.environment.get('bidId') || (b.bid && b.bid.id === pm.environment.get('bidId')));",
                  "pm.test('booking for the accepted bid is present', () => pm.expect(target).to.exist);",
                  "if (target && target.id) pm.environment.set('bookingId', target.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/me/provider/bookings/:id/start (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/provider/bookings/{{bookingId}}/start"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200/201/204', () => pm.expect([200, 201, 204]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/me/provider/bookings/:id/complete (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/provider/bookings/{{bookingId}}/complete"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200/201/204', () => pm.expect([200, 201, 204]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "08 — Notifications",
      "description": "The seeker should have notifications fired by the booking lifecycle (bid accepted, booking started, booking completed). Verifies the list endpoint and the unread-count.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/me/notifications (seeker)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{seekerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/notifications"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('at least one notification fired', () => pm.expect(body.items.length).to.be.greaterThan(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/me/notifications/unread-count (seeker)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{seekerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/notifications/unread-count"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('count is number', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().count).to.be.a('number'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "09 — Chat",
      "description": "Provider opens a conversation tied to the booking, sends a message, then reads the messages list back to confirm the round-trip.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/provider/conversations (provider — open)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/conversations",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"bookingId\": \"{{bookingId}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 201', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const conv = body.conversation || body;",
                  "pm.test('conversation.id present', () => pm.expect(conv.id).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('conversationId', conv.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/provider/conversations/:id/messages (provider — send)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
            ],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"body\": \"runtime chat round-trip\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200 or 201', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/provider/conversations/:id/messages (provider — readback)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('round-trip message present', () => {",
                  "  const has = body.items.some(m => typeof m.body === 'string' && m.body.indexOf('runtime chat round-trip') !== -1);",
                  "  pm.expect(has).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "10 — Earnings",
      "description": "After the booking is COMPLETED the provider's earnings summary should report ≥ 1 completed booking and a non-zero gross.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/provider/earnings/summary (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/earnings/summary"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('canonical earnings shape', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('grossEarnings');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('platformFees');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('netEarnings');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('availableBalance');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('pendingBalance');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('completedBookingsCount');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('completedBookingsCount ≥ 1', () => pm.expect(body.completedBookingsCount).to.be.at.least(1));",
                  "pm.test('netEarnings = grossEarnings − platformFees', () => pm.expect(body.netEarnings).to.eql(body.grossEarnings - body.platformFees));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/provider/earnings/transactions (provider)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
            },
            "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
            "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/earnings/transactions"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('all rows are BOOKING_COMPLETED', () => {",
                  "  for (const it of body.items) pm.expect(it.kind).to.eql('BOOKING_COMPLETED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
